  "result": "The gate returned **OK** for NRS_484B_587_2b on the fourth of six allowed runs: 15 witnesses pass, and the rule calls no other rule.\n\n**Rule** (`NRS_484B_587_2b.lean`):\n- **Who it covers:** the subject must be a vehicle under the DEF-NRS-484A-320 definition.\n- **When it applies:** the vehicle is moving, its footprint is on a controlled-access region, and neither exception holds:\n  - **Emergency (e1):** hazard lamps flashing, or an emergency vehicle with a warning lamp lit in any colour.\n  - **Subsection 3 (e2/e7/e10/e12–e18):** a listed vehicle on a paved shoulder that lies on a highway it occupies, where a `shoulder_use_permitted` sign governs the shoulder and its conditions hold. The listed vehicles are an emergency vehicle, an incident-management or coroner vehicle, a tow vehicle that is a motor vehicle, or a transit bus.\n- **The duty (e6):** the vehicle's footprint must never first reach from one lane into the neighbouring lane on a side where the first lane's marking is solid or double solid white, when one of the two lanes is governed by an entrance or exit sign and the other is not.\n- I declared no narrowings of my own; every choice follows the node's record.\n\n**Witnesses:** the 10 planned scenes plus five I added so that every part of the formula affects some result:\n- `branch_7`: an incident-management vehicle on the permitted shoulder (not applicable).\n- `branch_8`: an ordinary car crossing from the through lane into an exit lane (violated).\n- `branch_9`: hazard lamps flashing (not applicable).\n- `branch_10` and `branch_11`: both lanes entrance-governed, or both exit-governed (compliant).\n\n**Gate runs:**\n1. **WITNESS_FAIL:** the outer lanes' neighbours couldn't be decided, so `permit` and `blind` came out unknown. Giving every lane its position and the lane count fixed it.\n2. **WITNESS_FAIL again:** I started this run by mistake on unchanged files, so it used up one run and told me nothing new. Before that, a different command I tried was blocked because only the gate command is allowed; it never ran.\n3. **VACUOUS:** no scene tested the \"other lane has no entrance/exit sign\" condition. `branch_10` and `branch_11` cover it.\n4. **OK.**\n\nIn the shoulder scenes I stated the vehicle's overlap with the shoulder, ramp and through lane directly; the vehicle isn't built wide enough to physically span all three. The details are in `task_result.md` in the working directory.",
